15	// Two rows, the way dynamoLive keeps them: `marks` is the CONN row, written
16	// by connect() and read by connection() and decksOf(); `watchMarks` is the
17	// per-session row, written by watch() from its own attached argument and
18	// read by watchers(). A deck's watch row must carry `deck: true` on its
19	// own, the same as it does in dynamo, or a deck would look like a writer
20	// of the run it is watching. The watch row is dated too, as dynamo dates
21	// it, because which of an account's devices takes a press turns on it.
22	function memoryLive(): LiveStore & {
23	  conns: Map<string, string>;
24	  watches: Map<string, Set<string>>;
25	  marks: Map<string, Attached>;
26	  watchMarks: Map<string, Attached>;
